  "text": "Logarithm Logarithm, Log The logarithm of a number is the power the base of the logarithm has to be raised to in order to equal the number. If the base of the logarithm is 10 and the number is 1,000 then the log is 3 since 10 has to be raised to the 3rd power to equal 1,000. See anti-log",
